{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they heard the voice of YHWH Elohim walking in the garden in the wind of the day</b>. The Sages said (Genesis Rabbah 19:7): Rabbi Hilfi said, we have heard that sound has a walking, as it is written, \"And they heard the voice of YHWH Elohim walking in the garden.\" And thus the Rav wrote in the Guide for the Perplexed (I:24), and so too is the opinion of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 3:8), that \"walking\" (מִתְהַלֵּךְ) is an expression for sound, in the manner of \"her sound goes like the serpent\" (Jeremiah 46:22). And he said that the reason for \"in the wind of the day\" (לְרוּחַ הַיּוֹם) is that they heard the sound toward evening, and he mentioned in the name of Rabbi Yonah that the meaning is: and the man was walking in the garden in the wind of the day. In my opinion, the meaning of \"walking in the Garden of Eden\" is like the meaning of \"and I will walk in your midst\" (Leviticus 26:12), \"and YHWH went as He finished speaking to Abraham\" (Genesis 18:33), \"I will go and return to My place\" (Hosea 5:15), and this refers to the revelation of the Shekhinah in that place or its withdrawal from the place where it had been revealed. And the reason for \"in the wind of the day\" is that when the Shekhinah is revealed, a great and strong wind comes, as in the matter that is written (1 Kings 19:11): \"and behold, YHWH passed by, and a great and strong wind rending the mountains and breaking rocks before YHWH,\" and likewise \"and He rode upon the wings of the wind\" (Psalms 18:11), and it is written in Job (Job 38:1): \"And YHWH answered Job from the storm.\" Therefore Scripture says here that they heard the voice of YHWH, for the Shekhinah was revealed in the garden as though approaching them in the wind of the day, for the wind of YHWH blew in the garden like the wind of the days, not a great and strong wind as seen in the other prophecies, so that they would not be terrified and bewildered. And Scripture says that even so they hid themselves because of their treachery. And in Genesis Rabbah (19:7) they also said: Rabbi Abba bar Kahana said, it is not written \"walking\" (מְהַלֵּךְ) here but rather \"walking\" (מִתְהַלֵּךְ) — leaping and ascending. Behold, Rabbi Abba took it in the same sense as \"and YHWH went\" (וַיֵּלֶךְ ה'), just as we explained regarding the expression of going, except that he interpreted the verse for the withdrawal of the Shekhinah that had been dwelling in the Garden of Eden and withdrew from it because of the sin of the man, in the manner of \"I will go and return to My place,\" whereas we interpret it as the revelation of the Shekhinah in that place, and this is the correct and fitting interpretation in Scripture."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:20:52.725529881Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}